(text "Lira: nRF52840 (Ebyte E73-2G4M08S1C), USB-C + Li-Po, 57 keys, built-in USB sound card" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 18 0) (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "47217bbf-6d1d-4669-a79e-873b55fd7840"))
(text "Power / USB / programming copied from the BlueMicro840 (jpconstantineau/NRF52-Board), a board built with this module, assembled by JLCPCB and sold. Differences from it:" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 23 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7ab8186c-7f58-42c6-b456-3c5d70754273"))
(text "1. Second regulator (switched 3.3 V for external devices, P0.12 enable) omitted: nothing external to power." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7fa56db6-c1ee-41cd-b6eb-a4d6ff8cf7e6"))
(text "2. USBLC6-2SC6 ESD array added on D+ / D- / VBUS at the USB-C receptacle." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 30.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "11f49434-51ae-44fd-a6a2-f6ea7d287a81"))
(text "3. Power switch SW101 (C&K JS102011SAQN, 300 mA) in the battery + line, as on ZMK keyboards; JP2 bypasses it." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 33.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9eb994f3-0ac3-44a9-8212-11764b0515ef"))
(text "4. JP1 + R104: closing the solder jumper puts a second 10k on PROG: charge current 100 mA -> 200 mA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 36.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c96ec2b0-6665-40ee-8c99-7b45871db89b"))
(text "5. Reset push button SW102 to GND (the BlueMicro840 has only a test point)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 39.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b7f4f77e-bb61-45f8-a8a3-d5da2ca60a11"))
(text "6. USB-C shield pads to GND (left open on the BlueMicro840)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 43 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9e551ae3-b7cb-442e-8ae2-c5c1d7e7566e"))
(text "7. LEDs: charging LED white, status LED red on P1.04 only (BlueMicro840: green charging, red P1.04, blue P1.10)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 46.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d8383d44-5951-4e24-94ac-649cabca7a4f"))
(text "8. DCCH inductor pads (DNP on the BlueMicro840) not fitted at all; P1.10 is a free GPIO here, P1.02 switches the sound card." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 49.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a7fc709a-fe37-4483-b655-426297aad0be"))
(text "9. Test points added on VBUS, VBAT and VIN (BlueMicro840: SWDIO, SWCLK, VCC, GND, RESET, P1.02)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 52.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "fc495bc7-6e40-4731-b642-e605d9315315"))
(text "10. C107 4.7 uF added on VBUS at the charger's VDD pin (the MCP73831 datasheet asks for 4.7 uF; Nordic's reference circuit has 4.7 uF on VBUS; the BlueMicro840 has none)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 55.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1f01c87a-c4d3-48bf-9e38-025c1a8ca645"))
(text "11. C108 1 uF at the regulator output and C109 100 nF at the module: the 4.7 uF C103 sits at the module's supply pins (VDD / VDDH), 25 mm away (the module has about 12 uF inside: the TPS7A02 allows 1-22 uF on its output). C102 on VIN is 1 uF instead of 10 uF: together they keep the capacitance charged at USB attach near USB 2.0's 10 uF." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 59 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "572873bd-c770-418e-a1dc-382b34945a39"))
(text "12. Charger MCP73831 instead of the TP4054, same pins and same PROG resistor (1000 V / R_PROG): it is stable with no battery, so the board also works when built without one (its STAT pin, and the white LED, stay off)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 62.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8269947b-5714-47a0-8bee-7570699c1a8a"))
(text "13. Battery divider 10M + 10M with 10 nF (BlueMicro840: 806k + 2M, 1 nF): the MCP73831 recognises a missing battery only if VBAT sees more than 7 MOhm (datasheet 4.2); 10 nF >= 2^12 x the SAADC's 2.5 pF keeps the reading within 1 LSB (Nordic, 'Measuring Lithium battery voltage with nRF52'), and RMK samples it every 30 s. Drain 0.2 uA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 65.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7ce317df-ceec-40e7-8182-7648862ae629"))
(text "14. Built-in USB sound card: the USB-C data lines go (through the ESD array) to a CH334P hub; hub port 3 goes to the module's D+ / D-, port 2 to a CM108B codec (C-Media demo board v1.33) with a 3.5 mm headset jack." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 68.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9bce3d35-f34c-4762-b63a-6a3266153604"))
(text "15. Reverse-battery P-MOSFET Q2 (SI2301) between the battery connector and the switch, gate to GND: a cell plugged in the wrong way round finds it off (its body diode blocks), so the charger's VBAT pin never sees a negative voltage; the right way round it is on (Vgs = -Vbat) and charging goes through it." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 71.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "791df74b-3bf4-428f-8e52-1a3d4814fbbd"))
(text "16. Regulator TPS7A0233 (25 nA quiescent, 200 mA) instead of the AP2112K (55 uA): same SOT-23-5 pins (IN, GND, EN, NC, OUT); the 3.3 V rail needs < 50 mA (module, status LED)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 75 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "53e19311-2a87-4f0b-ab95-708b65c9cd3e"))
(text "17. VBUS: an SMF5.0A TVS at the receptacle, and C107 (4.7 uF) through 1 ohm: a ceramic-only VBUS rings on hot plug to 6-8 V through the cable's inductance (simulated, 0.5-1 uH); damped, 5.0-6.6 V, without adding capacitance." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22 78.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6b5312ed-5efe-49b8-8ef5-a037b2733fe6"))
(text "USB-C (sink: 5.1k on each CC) and ESD protection" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 83.59 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "74c3dbe9-e580-4001-901f-505db80a85af"))
