(global_label "GND" (shape passive) (at 393.7 361.95 0) (fields_autoplaced yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "4b5bb880-ca19-4b1e-932d-e6603ee9e04f") (property "Intersheetrefs" "${INTERSHEET_REFS}" (at 393.7 361.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (hide yes))))
(text "Differences from the C-Media demo board:" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 397.59 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0862e553-9834-41ec-85d2-46962e07d775"))
(text "1. Supply: VBUS through a TPS22919 load switch (soft start 1.3 ms, output discharge) to AUD_5V, ON = P1.02 with a 100k pull-down: the sound card is" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 400.89 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1320a8a2-fb8b-4a53-a804-5c5eb0a4e86b"))
(text "   powered only in USB mode (firmware src/audio_gate.rs). A hard switch-on would dip VBUS enough to reset the hub (CH334 datasheet 6.1)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 404.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "25efb224-0a41-42a3-aeac-11d6ba8eb9ef"))
(text "2. Headphones: a TPA6132A2 DirectPath amplifier after LOL / LOR (demo board: 100 uF + 39R straight to the jack): about 0 ohm output impedance, no" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 407.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b34c894d-dd35-4012-b101-2ee499f9251f"))
(text "   coupling capacitors, 0 dB gain (-6 dB with JP3 closed, for very sensitive earphones). Inputs single-ended through 1 uF (8 Hz); EN about 50 ms after" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 410.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8b750754-6659-46d5-a02d-ab386daae105"))
(text "   the supply (1M + 100 nF from P1.02, into the pin through 33k: EN may not exceed VDD + 0.3 V, and C137 still holds 3.3 V for a moment when the cable" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 414.09 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "74685a7f-339e-4f77-b304-ccf40623e905"))
(text "   is pulled) and off at once through a Schottky. The switch's output discharge goes through 1k (TPS22919 9.2.2.2): the 5 V falls in about 3 ms, so" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 417.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "68e99be0-55d9-46b0-ba05-bd9fff2008db"))
(text "   the amplifier is off before the codec loses its supply (TPA6132A2 p.12, no pop)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 420.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "faa087e4-30b0-4beb-9e4c-1343ae369023"))
(text "3. Amplifier off in USB suspend: the codec's PDSW (open drain, low in operation, open in suspend; app note 1.50) with a 100k pull-up to AUD_5V drives" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 423.99 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "271bcc1f-0632-49aa-bc3c-7154fe2216b2"))
(text "   a 2N7002 that holds the amplifier's EN low while the host sleeps (2 mA -> < 1 uA); the codec itself stays enumerated and draws its suspend current." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 427.29 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7fb6dd62-2e58-43e6-9d80-6d0de02c58ba"))
(text "4. Hub supply: V5 and VDD33 both on a 3.3 V regulator (TPS7A0233) fed from VBUS (CH334 datasheet 6.4), instead of V5 on VBUS: V5's absolute maximum is" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 430.59 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "852b0408-e3ff-4552-8e13-64fe8c426040"))
(text "   5.5 V and a USB hot plug rings above it; the regulator's input is rated 6.5 V. The regulator is on only with VBUS (the hub draws nothing from the" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 433.89 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f94ce70f-6edc-4e96-87dc-4e92b192f8af"))
(text "   battery)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 437.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b7003fac-9c96-4d8a-bd78-1e38cfd115f3"))
(text "5. Microphone: bias 1.2k + 2.2k (demo board 2.2k + 8.2k, for PC microphones) for phone headsets (Android: 1.8-2.9 V through 2.2k); 1k in series before" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 440.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1b5c6d29-f6b7-49fb-8045-290b7010b027"))
(text "   MICIN against the step when a plug goes in." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 443.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "af0dc9f5-96b7-4ff6-a3d6-974f6c1f8f00"))
(text "6. The demo board's two 10 nF capacitors DVDD - DREG18 and DVDD - DREG33 ('close to IC', for ESD) are fitted." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 447.09 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "55e14091-5699-4502-ac2a-03293bbb16c1"))
(text "7. The amplifier's SGND (pin 15) is grounded at the amplifier (its ground pad and a via into the top ground plane), not on a track of its own to the" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 450.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2706c24a-6daf-4612-b7fc-3ca5c0cc71fa"))
(text "   jack's ground pin as TI suggests (datasheet 10.3): with both layers poured the difference is a few millivolts." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 453.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a9e5a7d8-9fab-46d6-bfed-4105696ac7bf"))
(text "8. The four mode jumpers are also strapped with 10k (MODE/ADSEL low, PWRSEL/MSEL high to DREG33) on top of the chip's internal pulls. D105-D107 are" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 456.99 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1a41af15-5767-48a2-af4c-99074813cac0"))
(text "   bidirectional ESD clamps (PESD5V0S1BA) on the jack's left, right and microphone contacts: a DirectPath output swings below GND, so the clamp must" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 460.29 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b8222748-5441-4a8c-aaab-598ac21af872"))
(text "   be bidirectional." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 463.59 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9e73b55e-1f54-4a12-9a57-33de1ae01c82"))
(text "Key matrix, col2row: column -> switch -> diode (cathode on the row). Labels: (row,col) of each key." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 231.59 0) (effects (font (size 1.778 1.778) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1fb64f5f-94e2-47fa-bdb8-fd3012261497"))
